# Edge Function deploy commands (always paste the full string)

When an Edge Function must be redeployed (after you change `supabase/functions/**`, or after a migration that depends on Edge behavior), **always show the complete copy-pasteable command** in the reply. Never say only "redeploy send-discord" or "redeploy the Edge Function."

## Required reply format

Include a short fenced block with the exact command(s), for example:

```bash
npx supabase functions deploy send-discord --no-verify-jwt
```

If several functions changed, list **each full command** on its own line.

If the project is not linked yet in that shell, also show the one-time setup lines:

```bash
npx supabase login
npx supabase link --project-ref YOUR_PROJECT_REF
```

Use the real project ref only when it is already known from local config; otherwise leave `YOUR_PROJECT_REF`.

## Canonical deploy commands (this repo)

Source of truth: `docs/SUPABASE_SETUP.md` section Deploy Edge Functions. Prefer `npx supabase` (CLI is a devDependency).

| Function | Full command |
|---|---|
| `ban-user` | `npx supabase functions deploy ban-user` |
| `unban-user` | `npx supabase functions deploy unban-user` |
| `delete-account` | `npx supabase functions deploy delete-account` |
| `validate-rsi-handle` | `npx supabase functions deploy validate-rsi-handle` |
| `send-discord` | `npx supabase functions deploy send-discord --no-verify-jwt` |
| `log-watcher-webhook` | `npm run copy-blueprint-lookup` then `npx supabase functions deploy log-watcher-webhook --no-verify-jwt` |
| `discord-services-interactions` | `npx supabase functions deploy discord-services-interactions --no-verify-jwt` |
| `discord-services-dispatch` | `npx supabase functions deploy discord-services-dispatch` |
| `discord-services-expire` | `npx supabase functions deploy discord-services-expire --no-verify-jwt` |
| `discord-services-bot-invite` | `npx supabase functions deploy discord-services-bot-invite` |
| `discord-services-post-test` | `npx supabase functions deploy discord-services-post-test` |
| `manage-github-collaborator` | `npx supabase functions deploy manage-github-collaborator` |
| `link-citizenid` | `npx supabase functions deploy link-citizenid` |
| `citizenid-oauth-callback` | `npx supabase functions deploy citizenid-oauth-callback --no-verify-jwt` |
| `unlink-citizenid` | `npx supabase functions deploy unlink-citizenid` |

**Do not drop `--no-verify-jwt`** on functions that require it above (Discord cron/webhooks, log-watcher, services interactions/expire, `citizenid-oauth-callback`).

## When this applies

- Finishing work that edits an Edge Function
- Telling the user what to run after merge / after applying a related migration
- PR descriptions / Apply-deploy checklists that mention Edge redeploys

Also paste the matching migration filename when SQL must be applied first.
